    <entry>
        <title type="html"><![CDATA[Fix technical claims on the ARIA document role page]]></title>
        <id>https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/45931</id>
        <link href="https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/45931"/>
        <updated>2026-09-30T02:58:57.000Z</updated>
        <content type="html"><![CDATA[<img src="https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/198354403?v=4" width="64" height="64" alt=""/><br/><h3 dir="auto">Description</h3>
<p dir="auto">This PR corrects several technical claims on the ARIA <code class="notranslate">document</code> role page.</p>
<h3 dir="auto">Motivation</h3>
<ul dir="auto">
<li>The example placed a <code class="notranslate">document</code> inside a <code class="notranslate">dialog</code> and called the dialog a composite widget. <code class="notranslate">dialog</code> is a window role, and the spec says the <code class="notranslate">document</code> role only changes assistive technology behavior inside a widget or application. The example now uses <code class="notranslate">application</code>, which matches the spec's own example, and a short note explains why a dialog doesn't need the role.</li>
<li><code class="notranslate">aria-expanded</code> is not a supported state on the <code class="notranslate">document</code> role, so I removed it from the attribute list and from "Required JavaScript features".</li>
<li><code class="notranslate">tabindex</code> is an HTML attribute, so I removed it from the ARIA attribute list. The keyboard interactions section now links to it instead.</li>
<li>Best practices now mentions that <code class="notranslate">tabindex="0"</code> adds the element to the tab order, and that widgets using arrow-key focus management need to let users reach the document content and get back to the widget.</li>
<li>The comparison with <code class="notranslate">article</code> said <code class="notranslate">document</code> elements have no relation to each other. The spec doesn't say this, and the issue points out it could mislead authors, so I removed the paragraph.</li>
</ul>
<h3 dir="auto">Additional details</h3>
<ul dir="auto">
<li>Spec: <a href="https://w3c.github.io/aria/#document" rel="nofollow">document role</a> (supported states do not include <code class="notranslate">aria-expanded</code>) and <a href="https://w3c.github.io/aria/#window_roles" rel="nofollow">window roles</a>.</li>
<li><code class="notranslate">markdownlint-cli2</code> and <code class="notranslate">prettier --check</code> on the page report 0 issues, and the front-matter linter passes.</li>
<li>Previewed with <code class="notranslate">npm start</code>: the page renders with no flaws, and the new roving <code class="notranslate">tabindex</code> anchor resolves.</li>
</ul>
<h3 dir="auto">Related issues and pull requests</h3>
<p dir="auto"><span class="issue-keyword tooltipped tooltipped-se" aria-label="This pull request closes issue #33746.">Fixes</span> <a class="issue-link js-issue-link" data-error-text="Failed to load title" data-id="2316186464" data-permission-text="Title is private" data-url="https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/33746" data-hovercard-type="issue" data-hovercard-url="/mdn/content/issues/33746/hovercard" href="https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/33746">#33746</a></p>]]></content>
