        <title type="html"><![CDATA[Unify toJSON() methods' wording (1): performance API toJSON]]></title>
        <id>https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/45914</id>
        <link href="https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/45914"/>
        <updated>2026-09-28T22:31:39.000Z</updated>
        <content type="html"><![CDATA[<img src="https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/55398995?u=9f6a9837c9879eceb0abde487a338b92d4e206fc&v=4" width="64" height="64" alt=""/><br/><p dir="auto">Part of <a class="issue-link js-issue-link" data-error-text="Failed to load title" data-id="3208718025" data-permission-text="Title is private" data-url="https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/40230" data-hovercard-type="issue" data-hovercard-url="/mdn/content/issues/40230/hovercard" href="https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/40230">#40230</a>.</p>
<p dir="auto">"JSON object" is not a thing, and "JSON representation" is simply wrong: it returns a "JSON-serializable object".</p>
<p dir="auto">I am using the exact same wording as JS pages, such as <a href="https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/JavaScript/Reference/Global_Objects/Temporal/PlainDate/toJSON" rel="nofollow">https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/JavaScript/Reference/Global_Objects/Temporal/PlainDate/toJSON</a>, to explain how it's implicitly called:</p>
<blockquote>
<p dir="auto">The <code class="notranslate">toJSON()</code> method is automatically called by {{jsxref("JSON.stringify()")}} when an <code class="notranslate">InteractionContentfulPaint</code> object is stringified. This method is generally intended to, by default, usefully serialize <code class="notranslate">InteractionContentfulPaint</code> objects during <a href="/en-US/docs/Glossary/JSON">JSON</a> serialization.</p>
</blockquote>]]></content>
